## Vercel Web Analytics Implementation

Successfully implemented Vercel Web Analytics for this Next.js project following the latest official documentation from https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart

### Changes Made

**1. Package Installation**
- Installed `@vercel/analytics` package using npm
- Updated `package.json` with the new dependency
- Updated `package-lock.json` with the complete dependency tree

**2. Code Changes**
Modified `src/app/layout.tsx`:
- Added import statement: `import { Analytics } from "@vercel/analytics/next";`
- Added `<Analytics />` component inside the `<body>` tag, after the `</LanguageProvider>` closing tag
- Follows Next.js App Router best practices by placing Analytics in the root layout

**3. Implementation Details**
- This is a Next.js App Router project, so the Analytics component was added to the root layout file
- The component is placed at the end of the body, which is the recommended position according to Vercel's documentation
- The implementation uses the framework-specific import path `@vercel/analytics/next` for optimal Next.js integration

**4. Verification**
- ✅ Build completed successfully with `npm run build`
- ✅ Linter passed with no errors using `npm run lint`
- ✅ All routes compiled and generated correctly
- ✅ No TypeScript errors

### Next Steps
To enable analytics data collection:
1. Deploy this project to Vercel
2. Enable Web Analytics in the Vercel dashboard under the project's Analytics tab
3. Analytics data will automatically start being collected after deployment

### Files Modified
- `web/package.json` - Added @vercel/analytics dependency
- `web/package-lock.json` - Updated with dependency tree
- `web/src/app/layout.tsx` - Added Analytics import and component
